/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate32_vp_nEicosane -- the vapour pressure of nEicosane, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 steps 2 and 3).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate
  vp nEicosane`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00821          8 pts  313.15-343.15 K  Widegren; Beall; Tolbert; Lovestead et al.
      10.1021/je800534x                 6 pts  312.76-373.17 K  Razzouk; Naccoul; Mokbel; Saab et al.
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      (none)

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/acs.jced.6b00821 (8 pts, 313.15-343.15 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je800534x (6 pts,
  312.76-373.17 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 4.2 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 6 points (4.02 to 4.42 %, mean 4.181 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 616.95 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 312.76-373.17 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  OBJECTIVE (C281 step 3, declared): `objective { method twoStage; }` --
  Vitor's fitting practice (DEV.md 4c C280): least squares in log10 P for a
  first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in P, (P_model - P)/P, over
  the fit points minimised from it; both answers are kept in the result.  A
  student who prefers another objective declares `leastSquares` or `minimax`.

  EARLIER FIT, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 3.607758 - 1978.6123/(T + -123.7264),
  in-sample R2 0.999592 over 8 points, 313.15-343.15 K. HELD OUT: 6
  points, AAD 28.3788 % against the band 4.2 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 673.03 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 28.38 % against the band 4.2 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.280221 - 2250.4296/(T +
  -110.8773), in-sample R2 0.999299 over 8 points, 313.15-343.15 K. HELD
  OUT: 6 points, AAD 26.3951 % (max 34.2660 %) against the band 4.2 % ->
  notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares answer on the same points: AAD
  28.3788 %, max 36.2230 %. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  637.35 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict notValidated (AAD 26.4 %
  against the band 4.2 % declared before the fit); the record keeps
  AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  nEicosane;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/nEicosane-vapourPressure-acs.jced.6b00821.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/acs.jced.6b00821"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/nEicosane-vapourPressure-je800534x.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je800534x"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  4.2 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 6 points (4.02 to 4.42 %, mean 4.181 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        objective  { method twoStage; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
